# Experiment outputs stay on disk as-is

When the **save format, paths, filenames, or schema** of experiment outputs changes, modify only the **code/notebooks that produce them**.

## Do

- Update writers, serializers, path construction, and any related docs in source/notebooks.
- Assume future runs will produce the new layout; old runs keep their current files.

## Do not

- Rewrite, migrate, rename, delete, or regenerate experiment outputs already present on disk to match the new convention.
- Add one-off scripts whose only job is to convert historical experiment folders unless the user explicitly asks.

```text
# ❌ BAD — change how results are saved, then "fix up" existing experiment dirs
# ✅ GOOD — change the generating code only; leave on-disk experiment outputs alone
```
